---
title: Auto-Code Component Interaction & Communication Patterns
---
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber

    participant User as 👤 User
    participant Browser as 🌐 Web Browser
    participant ElectronUI as 🖥️ Electron<br/>Renderer (React)
    participant Preload as 🔒 Preload Bridge<br/>(contextBridge)
    participant MainProcess as ⚡ Electron<br/>Main Process
    participant WebFrontend as ⚛️ Web Frontend<br/>(React)
    participant WebBackend as 🌐 Web Backend<br/>(FastAPI)
    participant BackendCLI as 🐍 Backend CLI<br/>(Python)
    participant ClaudeSDK as 🤖 Claude SDK
    participant Database as 💾 Graphiti/LadybugDB

    %% ========================================
    %% Electron Desktop App IPC Communication
    %% ========================================

    Note over User,Database: 📱 ELECTRON DESKTOP APP - IPC COMMUNICATION

    User->>ElectronUI: 1. Click "Create New Spec"

    ElectronUI->>ElectronUI: 2. Call window.electronAPI.task.createSpec()
    Note right of ElectronUI: IPC call via exposed API<br/>(security boundary)

    ElectronUI->>Preload: 3. invoke('task:create-spec', data)
    Note right of Preload: contextBridge.exposeInMainWorld()<br/>Secure IPC channel

    Preload->>MainProcess: 4. ipcRenderer.invoke('task:create-spec')
    Note right of MainProcess: IPC Handler registered<br/>via ipcMain.handle()

    MainProcess->>MainProcess: 5. Validate request & permissions

    MainProcess->>BackendCLI: 6. spawn('python', ['spec_runner.py'])
    Note right of MainProcess: Child process with<br/>stdout/stderr streams

    BackendCLI->>ClaudeSDK: 7. Create agent session
    ClaudeSDK-->>BackendCLI: 8. Agent response

    BackendCLI->>Database: 9. Store spec & context
    Database-->>BackendCLI: 10. Confirmation

    BackendCLI-->>MainProcess: 11. JSON output via stdout
    Note left of BackendCLI: Stream-based communication<br/>newline-delimited JSON

    MainProcess->>MainProcess: 12. Parse stdout stream

    MainProcess-->>Preload: 13. IPC response + progress events
    Note left of MainProcess: event.sender.send()<br/>for progress updates

    Preload-->>ElectronUI: 14. Promise resolves with data

    ElectronUI->>ElectronUI: 15. Update Zustand state
    ElectronUI->>User: 16. Show success notification

    %% ========================================
    %% Web Application HTTP Communication
    %% ========================================

    Note over User,Database: 🌐 WEB APPLICATION - HTTP + WEBSOCKET COMMUNICATION

    User->>Browser: 17. Open web interface
    Browser->>WebFrontend: 18. Load React app

    WebFrontend->>WebBackend: 19. GET /api/specs (HTTP)
    Note right of WebFrontend: Fetch API<br/>REST HTTP request

    WebBackend->>WebBackend: 20. Authenticate JWT token

    WebBackend->>BackendCLI: 21. subprocess.run(['python', 'run.py', '--list'])
    Note right of WebBackend: Synchronous subprocess<br/>for quick operations

    BackendCLI-->>WebBackend: 22. JSON output via stdout

    WebBackend-->>WebFrontend: 23. HTTP 200 + JSON payload
    Note left of WebBackend: CORS headers included

    WebFrontend->>WebFrontend: 24. Update Zustand state
    WebFrontend->>Browser: 25. Render spec list

    Browser->>WebFrontend: 26. Click "Run Build"

    WebFrontend->>WebBackend: 27. WebSocket connect (ws://)
    Note right of WebFrontend: Real-time updates channel

    WebBackend-->>WebFrontend: 28. WebSocket connected

    WebFrontend->>WebBackend: 29. POST /api/specs/{id}/run (HTTP)

    WebBackend->>BackendCLI: 30. subprocess.Popen(['python', 'run.py'])
    Note right of WebBackend: Async subprocess with<br/>stdout/stderr streaming

    loop Real-time Progress Updates
        BackendCLI-->>WebBackend: 31. stdout stream (progress JSON)
        WebBackend-->>WebFrontend: 32. WebSocket message (progress)
        WebFrontend->>Browser: 33. Update progress UI
    end

    BackendCLI->>ClaudeSDK: 34. Agent operations
    ClaudeSDK-->>BackendCLI: 35. Agent responses

    BackendCLI->>Database: 36. Update session memory
    Database-->>BackendCLI: 37. Confirmation

    BackendCLI-->>WebBackend: 38. Process exit with status

    WebBackend-->>WebFrontend: 39. WebSocket message (complete)

    WebBackend-->>WebFrontend: 40. HTTP 200 + final result

    WebFrontend->>Browser: 41. Show completion notification

    %% ========================================
    %% Direct CLI Usage
    %% ========================================

    Note over User,Database: 💻 DIRECT CLI USAGE (No IPC/HTTP)

    User->>BackendCLI: 42. python run.py --spec 001
    Note right of User: Terminal command

    BackendCLI->>ClaudeSDK: 43. Create agent sessions
    ClaudeSDK-->>BackendCLI: 44. Agent responses

    BackendCLI->>Database: 45. Read/write memory
    Database-->>BackendCLI: 46. Data

    BackendCLI-->>User: 47. stdout/stderr output
    Note left of BackendCLI: Direct terminal output

    %% ========================================
    %% IPC Security Architecture
    %% ========================================

    Note over ElectronUI,MainProcess: 🔒 IPC SECURITY ARCHITECTURE

    rect rgb(255, 243, 224)
        Note over ElectronUI: RENDERER PROCESS (Untrusted)<br/>• No direct Node.js access<br/>• Context isolation enabled<br/>• nodeIntegration: false
    end

    rect rgb(255, 183, 77)
        Note over Preload: PRELOAD BRIDGE (Security Boundary)<br/>• contextBridge.exposeInMainWorld()<br/>• Whitelist-only API exposure<br/>• Input validation
    end

    rect rgb(129, 199, 132)
        Note over MainProcess: MAIN PROCESS (Trusted)<br/>• Full Node.js + Electron API<br/>• IPC handler validation<br/>• Process spawning control
    end

    %% ========================================
    %% HTTP API Patterns
    %% ========================================

    Note over WebFrontend,WebBackend: 🌐 HTTP API PATTERNS

    rect rgb(227, 242, 253)
        Note over WebFrontend: CLIENT-SIDE<br/>• Fetch API (REST)<br/>• WebSocket API (real-time)<br/>• JWT token in headers<br/>• Zustand state management
    end

    rect rgb(252, 228, 236)
        Note over WebBackend: SERVER-SIDE<br/>• FastAPI REST endpoints<br/>• CORS middleware<br/>• JWT authentication<br/>• WebSocket endpoint (/ws)<br/>• Subprocess management
    end

    %% Styling
    style User fill:#e3f2fd,stroke:#1976d2,stroke-width:2px
    style Browser fill:#e3f2fd,stroke:#1976d2,stroke-width:2px
    style ElectronUI fill:#ba68c8,stroke:#6a1b9a,stroke-width:2px,color:#fff
    style Preload fill:#ffb74d,stroke:#e65100,stroke-width:3px,color:#000
    style MainProcess fill:#81c784,stroke:#1b5e20,stroke-width:2px
    style WebFrontend fill:#f8bbd0,stroke:#c2185b,stroke-width:2px
    style WebBackend fill:#ef5350,stroke:#b71c1c,stroke-width:2px,color:#fff
    style BackendCLI fill:#66bb6a,stroke:#1b5e20,stroke-width:2px,color:#fff
    style ClaudeSDK fill:#4db6ac,stroke:#004d40,stroke-width:2px,color:#fff
    style Database fill:#26a69a,stroke:#004d40,stroke-width:2px,color:#fff
